/-!
# Ample generation and universally exact resolutions of finite locally free sheaves

On a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme `X` carrying an ample line bundle `L`, every
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F` of finite type is generated by finitely many global sections after
twisting by a sufficiently high tensor power `L^{⊗ p}` (`p ≥ N`), giving an epimorphism from a
finite direct sum of copies of `(L^{⊗ p})∨` onto `F` (Stacks, Lemma 28.26.13, Tag 01Q3).

For an epimorphism `π : P ⟶ E` of finite locally free sheaves on an arbitrary scheme `X`, the
kernel `K = ker(π)` is again finite locally free, and the short exact sequence `0 → K → P → E → 0`
splits locally on every affine open of `X`. Consequently, the dual sequence
`0 → E∨ → P∨ → K∨ → 0` remains exact after pullback along every scheme morphism `g : Y ⟶ X`.

Combining global generation by `L` with biduality and local splitting produces, for every finite
locally free sheaf `E` and every bound `N : ℕ`, a two-step resolution
`0 → E → ⨁_{Fin r} L^{⊗ p} → ⨁_{Fin s} L^{⊗ q}` with `p, q ≥ N` whose pullback along every
scheme morphism `g : Y ⟶ X` is a kernel. This is the geometric resolution input to the formal
completion criterion for finite locally free sheaves (Stacks, Lemma 52.15.1, Tag 0EKP).

## Main results

* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteLocallyFreeSheaf.isFiniteLocallyFree_kernel_of_epi`: the kernel
  of an epimorphism of finite locally free sheaves is finite locally free.
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteLocallyFreeSheaf.isLimitPullbackDualOfEpi`: for an
  epimorphism `π : P ⟶ E` of finite locally free sheaves with kernel `ι : K ⟶ P`, the pullback of
  `E∨ → P∨ → K∨` along any scheme morphism is a kernel.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_epi_biproduct_dual_tensorPow_of_isAmple`: global
  generation of a quasi-coherent finite-type module by an arbitrarily high power of an ample line
  bundle (Stacks, Tag 01Q3).
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteLocallyFreeSheaf.exists_universallyExact_ample_resolution`:
  every finite locally free sheaf on a quasi-separated scheme with an ample line bundle admits a
  universally exact two-step resolution by finite direct sums of arbitrarily high powers of `L`.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 0EKP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EKP)
-/

